  "worked_solution": "The difference $S-T$ consists of all the elements that are in $S$ but not $T.$ To represent $S-T,$ we will shade in all the area that is contained in $S$ but not $T.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037357/assets/c3694dbc8f5eb9bdaf352fc3d456c6dabc07224f18e73257a9030000e5b1263e.png)\n\nThe elements $a$ and $b$ are in $S$ but not $T.$\n\nTherefore, the difference is\n\n$$\nS-T={a,b}.\n$$",
